{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":61539,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"769a4141-7b1a-5c0c-b5ea-08af1a260256","total_cost_usd":0.31649000000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":12650,"output_tokens":5883,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5883,"cache_read_input_tokens":12650,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9600,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00967,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5883,"cacheReadInputTokens":12650,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30682000000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:stage1-recovery-fable-02\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires a selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (complete domain of 96 scheduled stations).\", \"observed_value\": \"complete-domain requirement\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Selected result uses the complete-domain denominator of 96 scheduled stations, not the 72-station retained subset.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/96 = 0.1875\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Workflow constructs the selected line dividing OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES by SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), confirming the complete-domain denominator in code.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator variable = SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Report explicitly keeps the 24 omitted stations in the denominator with zero occurrences, matching complete-domain exposure accounting.\", \"observed_value\": \"24 omitted stations retained in denominator\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification check: the numerator (18) is counted only among retained stations, which could suggest subset-based accounting; however, hand-counting inputs/data.csv occurrence_flag=1 rows yields exactly 18 (6 North, 6 Central, 6 South, 0 Outer), 72 retained rows, and 96 scheduled data rows across L0002-L0097, and the omitted stations have occurrence_flag=NA, so 18 is the total observed occurrences in the complete domain and 18/96 is the correct complete-domain rate given the visible data; the lower-bound caveat is explicitly stated.\", \"observed_value\": \"counts verified: 96 scheduled, 72 retained, 18 occurrences\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 11, \"quoted_text\": \"Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to show the selected rate secretly used the 72-station retained subset: I recomputed from inputs/data.csv (96 station rows L0002-L0097; 72 rows with screen_status=retained; 18 rows with occurrence_flag=1) and checked the arithmetic 18/96 = 0.1875, matching the reported value; 18/72 would have been 0.25, which is not reported anywhere in the selected result. The attempt failed to demonstrate the in-scope issue: the denominator is the complete 96-station scheduled domain as the task requires.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The stated scientific task is explicitly conditional on the retained subset (stations passing the signal screen), so a retained-subset denominator is the required domain, not a mismatch.\", \"observed_value\": \"task target is screen-conditional\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report declares the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations and the selected claim is phrased conditionally ('Among signal-eligible stations'), matching the 72-station denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/72 = 25% conditional claim\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Input data semantics confirm 18 eligible with occurrence plus 54 eligible without occurrence equals 72 eligible stations, matching the denominator used.\", \"observed_value\": \"18 + 54 = 72\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"signal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification check: the report also mentions the 96-station scheduled network and 24 stations outside the eligible set, which could tempt a complete-domain reading; however, those 24 are described as 'not assessed' and no claim in the report asserts a rate over the full 96-station network, so no complete-domain claim exists to mismatch the 72 denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"96-station context present but no complete-domain rate claimed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"outside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to find any reported claim asserting a complete-domain (96-station) rate paired with the 72-station denominator: I read every report line and the workflow's RESULT_LINE construction; the only rate claim is explicitly 'Among signal-eligible stations' with denominator 72, and the task itself defines the question as conditional on passing the screen. The attempt failed: the target is explicitly conditional on the retained subset, which the scope definition excludes from the issue class. Arithmetic check 18/72 = 25% is also consistent.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The selected result claims an occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network' (a 96-station complete domain per the task and the report's own stated target population) but computes it as 18/72 = 0.25 using only the 72 stations retained after the signal screen as the exposure denominator; the complete-domain computation consistent with the visible data would use all 96 scheduled stations (18/96 = 0.1875). This is limited to the denominator/claim-domain mismatch in the selected result; no other aspect of the workflow is judged.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow builds the selected line with SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) as the divisor while the claim text and stated scientific target assert the entire 96-station scheduled network, substituting a retained-subset exposure denominator for the required complete domain without any conditional restatement of the claim or approved deviation.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (complete domain).\", \"observed_value\": \"complete-domain requirement\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Report states the target population is all 96 scheduled stations, yet the selected result labeled for the entire network divides by only the 72 retained stations.\", \"observed_value\": \"claim domain = 96; denominator = 72\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Workflow code confirms the selected line divides by SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72), not SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), while asserting the entire-network domain in the claim text.\", \"observed_value\": \"divisor variable = SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 7, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Data confirm the complete domain is 96 scheduled stations (every row has scheduled=yes), of which 24 are omitted by the screen; e.g., an omitted scheduled station.\", \"observed_value\": \"96 scheduled rows; omitted stations exist within the scheduled domain\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 97, \"end_line\": 97, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification check: the report transparently discloses the 72-station retained-subset denominator, which could be read as conditioning the claim on the subset; however, the claim sentence itself asserts the rate is 'for the entire scheduled survey network', and disclosure of the denominator does not restate the claim as conditional on the retained subset.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator disclosed but claim remains complete-domain\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Falsification check: I looked for an approved deviation or amendment that could legitimately redefine the domain to the retained subset; the report explicitly states none exists.\", \"observed_value\": \"no amendment or approved deviation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to defeat the issue in three ways: (1) checked whether 72 could itself be the complete scheduled domain — inputs/data.csv contains 96 station rows (L0002-L0097), all with scheduled=yes, so the complete domain is 96 and 72 is a screen-retained subset; (2) checked whether the selected claim is explicitly conditional on the retained subset — the claim text asserts 'for the entire scheduled survey network' and the report's target population line states all 96 stations, so it is not conditional; (3) checked for an approved protocol deviation redefining the domain — the report states none exists. All three attempts failed, so the retained-subset-for-complete-domain mismatch stands (18/72 reported where the complete-domain rate would be 18/96).\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":16446,"ttft_stream_ms":1368,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":62136,"uuid":"476b12ed-c79c-4106-9097-30c408b8e6aa"}
